# Language & Documentation

## English only (code)

All of the following MUST be English:

- Identifiers: variables, functions, components, files
- Comments and TSDoc
- Commit messages (when you write them)

UI copy shown to users may stay French (or follow `src/lib/i18n.ts` / `src/lib/landing-copy.ts`). Do not mix French into code identifiers.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
/** Crée une salle duo */
export function creerSalle(duree: number) {}

// ✅ GOOD
/** Creates a duo room with the given duration in minutes. */
export function createDuoRoom(durationMinutes: number) {}
```

## TSDoc

Add `/** ... */` on complex utilities, hooks, and shared components. Cover:

- Intent (why it exists)
- Parameter constraints
- Security notes (auth, secrets, user-controlled input)

Skip TSDoc on trivial presentational components and obvious one-liners.
